h the increased productivity of the bottling machines. In order not to have the machines idle, the Ottakringer brewery is also licensed to bottle other products such as RedBull and Pepsi. It is the only big bottling facility left in Vienna and bottles 22 bottles (or 11 liters) per second.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4212\/3324051633.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Beer production can no longer keep up with the increased productivity of the bottling machines. In order not to have the machines idle, the Ottakringer brewery is also licensed to bottle other products such as RedBull and Pepsi. It is the only big bottling facility left in Vienna and bottles 22 bottles (or 11 liters) per second.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4206.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"After the Second World War, because &quot;lager&quot; was used for short instead of concentration camp, Lager beer was renamed to M\u00e4rzen beer. They chose the name M\u00e4rzen because March (m\u00e4rz) was the last month that you had ice to store the beer at -1 degree Celsius.\" data-attachment-id=\"39\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"After the Second World War, because &quot;lager&quot; was used for short instead of concentration camp, Lager beer was renamed to M\u00e4rzen beer. They chose the name M\u00e4